<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n11356" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Cōrycus</span></b>  or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">-ŏs</span></b> , i,
			m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Κώρυκος</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a promontory in
				Cilicia, with a town and harbor of the same name, and a cave,
				very celebrated in ancient times; also famous for its production
				of saffron;</i> now <i>Khorgos</i>, Mel 1, 13, 2;
				<i><span class="en">Plin.
				5, 27, 22, § 92</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Cic. Fam.
				12, 13, 2</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Liv. 33, 20, 4 al.</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Corycus mons,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sen. Q. N. 3, 11, 2</span></i>
			.—Hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Cōry-cĭus</span></b> , a,
			um, <i>adj., Corycian</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">specus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Mel.
					1, 13, 3</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">antra,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					31, 2, 20, § 30</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">crocus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Hor.
					S. 2, 4, 68</span></i>
			; cf. <i><span class="en">Plin. 21, 6, 17, § 31</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">in the same sense, nimbus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Mart.
					9, 39</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">and, comae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Stat. S. 5, 1, 214</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">senex,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					G. 4, 127</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>III.</b>
			Corycus, <i>a promontory and harbor on the coast of
				Ionia</i>, now <i>Ko/raka</i>, <i><span class="en">Liv. 37,
				12, 10</span></i>; <i><span class="en">36,
				43, 13</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>IV.</b>
			<i>A town in Pamphylia</i>,
				<i><span class="en">Eutr. 6, 31</span></i>.</div>
